# WS two-message guest echo over the production listener.
#
# Captured by driving the REAL `qqqai serve` binary (debug build of this tree)
# over real loopback TCP against the live-probe fixture project
# (qqq.toml with a kind = "ws" /ws route, echo-http.wat guest).
# Client bytes are fixed literals (same as production_serve_live_transcript):
# Sec-WebSocket-Key dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ==, masked hello-ws / second-message.
# The digest pins the server response bytes below: the 101 head plus the
# three server frames (echo 1, echo 2, close echo), concatenated in order.
# Reparse the hex dumps and rehash to verify.

